n('csharp/PfpLab.Client/CoreProcess.cs','process_boundary','Discovers/overrides interpreter, launches shared Python stdio core with UTF-8 pipes, bounded-count stderr tail and asynchronous shutdown/kill. No protocol arithmetic. Disposal tests cover ordinary exit; they are not an all-environment termination proof; tail count does not bound line bytes.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Client/JsonRpcChannel.cs','transport_boundary','Serializes requests, checks matching version/id, maps errors, faults after timeout/EOF/cancellation/IO. Timeout begins after acquiring semaphore, so queue wait is not included. ReadLineAsync has no response-byte cap. Protocol validation is a bounded subset, not independent replay.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Client/PfpLabClient.cs','client_facade','Five typed methods delegate to the one Python core; Run returns validated DTO plus raw JSON, Verify asks Python to replay. Pack JSON is extracted without full ScenarioIn validation. Local JSON parse adds no mathematical evidence.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Client/Dtos.cs','wire_contract','Checks presence, rational spelling and selected structure. It does not mirror all schema constraints: digest checks only length, verdict status/move are free strings, several missing value fields get deserializer defaults. Its 64-character output rational check rejects valid computed core values.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Client/Rational.cs','exact_value_adapter','BigInteger canonical parser/formatter/comparison with gcd and positive denominator; denominator-minus-one makes default zero. Exact for accepted spellings, but input MaxChars=64 is incorrectly reused to admit computed outputs; no general Python-output closure.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Desktop/MainViewModel.cs','ui_orchestration','Loads/edits/runs/saves/verifies via IPfpLabClient; presents exact strings, typed failures and cancellable commands. Existing results survive editing and failed runs. No independent calculation, checker or proof; mocks test orchestration only.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Desktop/Shell.cs','ui_process_lifecycle','WPF startup, process ownership, dialogs, selection events, cancellation and fail-closed unexpected exception handler. Static read plus build only; no interactive UI test. Historical score openly records eight surviving shell mutants.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Desktop/App.xaml','ui_layout','WPF resources and colors only. No protocol values or invariants are computed.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Desktop/MainWindow.xaml','ui_layout','Scenario editor, run controls and bound receipt/result grid. Displays core output; no independently computed mathematical state.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Tests/Harness.cs','test_harness','Named async test runner with assertions and aggregate exit 0/3; catches failed tests and prints summaries. No per-test timeout or theorem-level coverage guarantee.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Tests/Program.cs','test_entrypoint','Selects 22 unit/view-model checks or all 29 checks; does not launch the WPF application window.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Tests/UnitTests.cs','bounded_tests','Canonical rational examples, large integer comparison, DTO examples, scripted RPC errors/timeouts/cancellation and interpreter discovery. Sample receipt deliberately has incomplete scenario shape; 64-character nonhex digest and >64-character computed outputs are absent from tests.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Tests/ContractTests.cs','bounded_integration_tests','Seven real Python-core checks cover paper numbers, typed refusals, receipt exchange and process lifetime. Schema comparison checks field names only. Both language routes invoke the same Python computation, so this is transport/replay interoperability, not two independent mathematical implementations.')
n('csharp/PfpLab.Tests/ViewModelTests.cs','bounded_mock_tests','Seven mocked-client tests cover state/status/cancellation/save/verify behaviors and owned temporary files. Fake values establish no core correctness; no GUI event-loop interaction is tested.')
n('pfp_lab/core/admission.py','input_admission','Canonical fullmatch ASCII name/rational gates, exact-int rejection of bool/float, bounded input lengths and typed errors. Fraction values are exact. These input-size restrictions do not bound all computed rational output lengths.')
n('pfp_lab/cli/main.py','command_boundary','Shared-core commands, MAX_JSON_BYTES+1 capped file reads, stable exit codes and UTF-8 stdio framing. CLI success means a scenario ran, even when moves are refused. Schema export is structural and does not prove generated schema equivalence to validators.')
n('pfp_lab/cli/rpc.py','rpc_boundary','Five methods and strict envelope mapping to shared-core admission/run/replay. A full line is read before byte-length rejection; the input cap is not a preallocation memory bound. Unexpected exceptions terminate the process.')
n('pfp_lab/web/app.py','http_boundary','Stateless FastAPI routes delegate to shared core; streamed body cap, fixed asset allow-list and loopback-default bind guard. Remote use requires explicit flag and has no authentication. Synchronous bounded search inside async routes is not a latency guarantee; HTTP runtime recheck timed out.')
n('pfp_lab/web/static/app.js','ui_rendering','Edits JSON, loads packs, renders exact core strings, downloads last receipt and asks backend to verify uploads. Chart alone converts rationals to floating point; it plots attempted verdict.defect_after, including rejected proposals and both D and Phi_1 metrics. No browser-side independent checker or cancellation/order guard.')
n('pfp_lab/web/static/index.html','ui_layout','Accessible labels, editor, graph and result trace structure. Chart caption Defect after each step overstates the meaning of attempted and mixed-metric verdict values; no logic or formal evidence.')
n('pfp_lab/web/static/app.css','ui_style','Responsive/dark styles, grid/layout and result colors; no computation or mathematical claim. Static source review does not substitute for interactive visual/accessibility testing.')
for path in ['pfp_lab/__init__.py','pfp_lab/cli/__init__.py','pfp_lab/core/__init__.py','pfp_lab/tests/__init__.py','pfp_lab/web/__init__.py']:
    n(path,'empty_package_marker','Verified zero bytes: Python package marker with no semantic implementation or mathematical contribution.')

